)

The packed form is obtained by splitting the ID into two 7-bit groups: the upper group becomes the high byte and the
lower group the low byte. For instance, `PROGRAM` (ID `0x84`) has packed type `0x0104`.

== Objects (`KFObject`)

`KFObject` is the abstract base of every object read from a file. It stores:

- `data`: the raw bytes of the object (`RawData`), with their position in the file,
- `type`: the `KObject` value,
- `name`: the object name, set by the deserializer,
- `objectId`: the object ID inside its type.

Its Jackson annotations allow JSON serialization with a `type` property. Only three subclasses are registered for
polymorphic JSON: `KFProgram`, `KFSoundBlock` and `KFKeyMap`.

== Programs (`KFProgram`)

A program is a tree of segments. Each segment starts with a tag byte that identifies its type. `ProgramSegmentType`
lists them with their tag, size and the original `.h` file they come from:

