    [`MASTSEGTAG`], [`0x01`], [72], [`KFMasterSegment`],
    [`CHANSEGTAG`], [`0x02`], [16], [`KFChannelSegment`],
    [`ZONESEGTAG`], [`0x03`], [16], [`KFZoneSegment`],
    [`ARPSEGTAG`], [`0x04`], [26], [`KFArpSegment`],
    [`PGMSEGTAG`], [`0x08`], [16], [`KFProgramCommon`],
    [`LYRSEGTAG`], [`0x09`], [16], [`KFLayerSegment`],
    [`EFXSEGTAG`], [`0x0F`], [8], [`KFEfxSegment`],
    [`ASRSEGTAG`], [`0x10`], [8], [`KFAsrSegment`],
    [`LFOSEGTAG`], [`0x14`], [8], [`KFLfoSegment`],
    [`FCNSEGTAG`], [`0x18`], [4], [`KFFcnSegment`],
    [`ENCSEGTAG`], [`0x20`], [16], [`KFEncSegment`],
    [`ENVSEGTAG`], [`0x21`], [16], [`KFEnvSegment`],
    [`ATKSEGTAG`], [`0x27`], [16], [`KFEncSegment`],
    [`CALSEGTAG`], [`0x40`], [32], [`KFCalvinSegment`],
    [`HOBSEGTAG`], [`0x50`], [16], [`KFHobbesSegment`],
    [`FXRTSEGTAG`], [`0x68`], [8], [`KFFXRootTableSegment`],
    [`FXPTSEGTAG`], [`0x69`], [8], [`KFFXPartSegment`],
    [`HAMSEG1TAG`], [`0x78`], [32], [`KFHammSegment1`],
    [`HAMSEG2TAG`], [`0x79`], [32], [`KFHammSegment2`],
    [`HAMSEG3TAG`], [`0x7A`], [32], [`KFHammSegment3`],
  ),
  caption: [Program segments declared in `ProgramSegmentType`],
)

A raw tag is not always the base tag. When a segment type appears several times, the tag values are consecutive: for
instance `CALSEGTAG` is `0x40` and the next instances are `0x41`, `0x42`... The low part of the raw value is the
instance ID, and the type is found from the base tag. `ProgramSegmentIdentifier` stores both values.

== Sound blocks (`KFSoundBlock`)

A sound block describes a sample. It contains the sample headers (`KFSoundBlockHeader`), which give the sample rate,
the start and the length of the PCM data, and then the envelope list (`KFSoundBlockEnvelope`, each made of six signed
16-bit values: attack, decay and release rates and levels).

== Key maps (`KFKeyMap`)

A keymap links the keys of the keyboard to sound blocks. Its fields are described in the Part I (format) chapter. In
memory, each entry is a `KeyMapEntry`.

== Other types

The following classes exist in the model but are not registered for polymorphic JSON:

- `KFStudio` (type `STUDIO`),
- `KFMasterParameter`, with its `MDB`, `ZDB` and `CDB` blocks (type `TABLE`),
- `KFVelocityMap` and `KFPressureMap` (types `VELOCITY_MAP` and `PRESSURE_MAP`),
- `KFIntonationTable` (type `INTONATION_TABLE`).

== File container (`KurzweilFile`)

`KurzweilFile` is a record that groups the three parts of a loaded file:

